    {
      "id": "text",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "While the summer heat seeped into autumn, I spent my days moving around Eastern China. Hangzhou's lakesides rippled into Wenzhou's sweeping mountains. Nanjing's imperial history rolled into Shanghai's neon nightlife. There was a constant sense of movement. It's admirable, in a way. Even when at peace walking amongst more rural mountains, or the juxtaposing city-center lights, the current never really stopped — it just changed shape."
    },
